    <div class="guide-card">
      <h2>State-Specific Regulations</h2>
      <p>
        While central motor vehicle laws apply nationwide, states may have additional regulations 
        regarding permits, taxes, and entry restrictions. Always check local requirements when 
        operating in a new state.
      </p>

      <h3>Environmental Compliance</h3>
      <p>
        Vehicles must meet Bharat Stage (BS) emission norms. Currently, BS-VI is the standard for 
        all new vehicles. Older vehicles must maintain valid PUC certificates and may face 
        restrictions in certain cities.
      </p>

      <h3>Staying Updated</h3>
      <p>
        Transport regulations are frequently updated. Subscribe to RTO notifications, join 
        transport associations, and consult with legal experts to ensure continued compliance.
      </p>
